        "original_id": "80f79955-b8bc-58fe-a398-1ff6e6d204d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dennis Potter, Daniil Kharms, Roger Spottiswoode\n- Works: Mesmer, Clownery, Situations\n- Roles: television dramatist, screenwriter, journalist, poet, writer, dramatist, director\n\nFacts:\n- Daniil Kharms was born on 30 December 1905 and died on 2 February 1942.\n- Daniil Kharms was an early Soviet-era surrealist and absurdist poet, writer, and dramatist.\n- Dennis Potter was born on 17 May 1935 and died on 7 June 1994.\n- Dennis Potter was an English television dramatist, screenwriter, and journalist.\n- Mesmer is a 1994 Austrian-Canadian-British-German biographical film.\n- Roger Spottiswoode directed Mesmer from a script by Dennis Potter.\n- Clownery is based on the novel Situations by Daniil Kharms.",
